    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39118" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιδαψῐλεύω</span></b> , intr., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>abound, be abundant</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ister
				43
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Συβαριτικοὶ λόγοι</span>
			: but more commonly, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>. 
				Med.
			, <i>lavish upon</i> a person, <i>bestow freely</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς ἑωυτῶν μητέρας καὶ τὰς ἀδελφεὰς
					ὑμῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.20
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.400
			</span></i>; [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰν δαπάναν</span>] <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
				1.327.7
			</span></i> (Callatis, <span class="entity">i A.D.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ.
				τινί τοῦ γέλωτος</span>
			<i>give</i> him <i>freely of</i> it, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				2.2.15
			</span></i>: metaph., <i>illustrate more richly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DMort.</u>
				30.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>. intr.,
				<i>to be lavish</i>, Arist <i><span class="en">
				<u>VV</u>
				1250b25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.170
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔν τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					6.2
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Pr.Im.</u>
				14
			</span></i>.</div>
